{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== S1 mica-governing-buck CLOSED — RP-02 SLICE 1 COMPLETE AND LANDED ON MAIN ===\nLanded commits (all on origin/main, each LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, submitted individually per the AGENTS.md no-feature-branch fallback): 4758d47f82 Add the byte-preserving binding repository (T1, Gerrit 1880); 1429cb8d4b Delegate binding persistence to the repository (T2, Gerrit 1885 PS3); 0c318685c8 Record binding-store ownership in ADR 0099 (T3, Gerrit 1887). Net: binding_store.py 799 -> 710 LOC (off the 800 cap), new binding_repository.py 360 LOC, ADR 0099 289 lines, ~40 new tests.\n\nS1 CLOSE GOTCHA worth carrying forward: the first close attempt FAILED completion verification with 'No ADR covering the BindingRepository extraction was found in docs/adr/'. Cause was mine, not the verifier's: I had run git reset --hard origin/main BEFORE T3's merge replicated to the GitHub mirror, so my worktree HEAD was e9969f8aec which predates ADR 0099 — the verifier reads the worktree HEAD, so it correctly saw the ADR as absent. Fetching again (origin/main now 0c318685c8) and re-resetting made the close pass immediately. Lesson: after Submit, WAIT for mirror replication and confirm the artifact with git cat-file -e HEAD:<path> before invoking a close that verifies it. Also note story-level closes run the agentic completion verifier and can exceed 10 minutes; one attempt aborted a runaway tool-call loop at 68.9s/28 requests and auto-resume retried once.\n\nRESIDUAL-GAP DISPOSITIONS SO FAR (the full Phase-5 sweep belongs with the epic close):\nFILED: smalltime-rapid-elk (8384-f31f-f16f-4f14) bug — binding lifecycle alerts never dedupe because records omit timestamp_ns so is_deduped's 24h window can never match; linked discovered_from vivacious-widish-indianabat. Pinned rather than fixed in T1 because that slice was a byte-for-byte extraction.\nFILED: best-kingly-monkey (01d8-c18d-b229-419a) task — retarget RP-04 S7.3.a's config reads to binding_lifecycle.py after RP-02 S2 moves _env_int and RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE; linked discovered_from brainy-cooked-hog and relates_to insincere-illogical-antlion. This is the durable artifact the coordinator asked for, since the cross-epic constraint is advisory (soft relates_to, not enforced).\nACCEPTED: T2 review-plan G1G2 advisory (prio 0.667 vs 0.70) — 'BindingRepository does not exist' was an artifact of reviewing against origin/main before T1 landed; the depends_on edge already gave traceability and editing the description would have staled a freshly-earned attestation. Self-resolved when T1 landed.\nACCEPTED: P6 ac-quality advisories on T2 and T3 (prio 0.40, tool-bucketed 'defer') and T3's G6 (prio 0.298) — minor AC phrasing; editing would stale attestations for no behavioral gain.\nFIXED IN SCOPE: both T2 LLM-Review advisories (change-detector coupling in my own tests — rendered-annotation assertions and an exact ordered call trace) were applied, not deferred.\nNOT A GAP, resolved: the macOS test_repo_isolation_guard flake I recheck'd around is now fixed on main by 9f7407bb3d 'Isolate nested pytest basetemps'.\n\n=== EXACT RESUME POINT ===\nNEXT: S2 brainy-cooked-hog (fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb), now UNBLOCKED by the S1 close, status open, attestation UNSIGNED. Sequence: rebar review-plan fc1c (must be run only now that S1 is closed, else it fast-fails as blocked), remediate any blocking finding, claim, then run its three tasks in this linear order — T1 dermatoid-brassy-junco (6083, identity transitions), T2 sportive-statued-goose (f59b, absence/tombstone/comment policy), T3 morose-selfaware-unicorn (2419, the narrow note_rich_emit facade operation). Each task is also UNSIGNED and must earn review-plan in dependency order as its predecessor closes. Then S3 convergent-pinelike-lunamoth (486a) with T1 polarized-servile-jenny (c4f7), T2 flamboyant-possessive-blackbuck (90a5), T3 likeminded-wearproof-barracuda (ef69). Then the epic, whose close requires the full residual-gap sweep above.\nBINDING CONSTRAINTS FOR THE REMAINING WORK, all verified against the code, not assumed:\n1. S2 MUST add binding_lifecycle.py entries to scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py in the SAME change for BOTH moved reads (os.environ.get and RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE), or make lint fails and the PRE-COMMIT HOOK blocks the commit before any push. Preserve ambient sourcing byte-identically (same defensive parse, default 3, clamp minimum 1) — do NOT cut to a config seam, that is RP-04's slice. Retarget/remove the stale binding_store.py rows so the registry stays truthful. Add scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py to fc1c via set-file-impact (it is NOT in the recorded impact) and note the move in ADR 0099.\n2. S3 T2's run_differs.py edit is the INVOCATION ONLY; the classifier lives in binding_recovery.py. run_differs.py is 739/800 with 61 lines of headroom.\n3. S3 T3 keeps its diff tight to _observe_rich_reemit (apply_handlers.py ~223-273) and its docstring; do NOT reflow the adjacent _rich_cutover_active (~210-214). The docstring at ~250-256 asserting that binding_store.py 'sits at the module-size cap and cannot carry a narrower accessor' becomes FALSE once S2 T3 adds note_rich_emit — update it in the same change as a direct non-behavioral comment-accuracy fix, no manufactured test. RP-04 S3 (6e3b) is CLOSED so the rebase precondition is satisfied.\n4. Keep all new modules free of load_config(); make lint now runs BOTH config gates (check_config_ownership.py and check_config_reads.py).\n5. Regenerate docs/env-vars.md with scripts/gen_env_registry.py whenever a module restructure shifts a non-literal env read's line.\n6. Every intermediate commit must satisfy the strictly-greater-than 800 cap; near-cap warning band starts at 720.\n7. Amending with git commit --amend -F <file> MUST carry the existing Change-Id trailer forward, or Gerrit opens a new change (this cost an abandoned 1883).\n8. Close descriptions: tick AC boxes ONLY, never add text — box state is normalized out of the attestation fingerprint but any text edit stales it.\nWORKTREE: /Users/joeoakhart/impl-rp02-binding-store on branch impl-rp02-binding-store, currently clean at origin/main 0c318685c8. Held-out oracles and mutation harnesses preserved under /tmp/rp02-heldout/ (gate.sh <change-number> reports Gerrit label state)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787113563463592001,"uuid":"b41c594f-e7d2-44c1-b6e5-cfc04185a955"}